    _createStaticVNode("<p class=\"module-kicker\">Module 7 - Role-based tools</p><h1 id=\"genesys-ai-for-call-center-excellence\" tabindex=\"-1\">Genesys AI for Call-Center Excellence <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#genesys-ai-for-call-center-excellence\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Genesys AI for Call-Center Excellence&quot;\">​</a></h1><p class=\"module-lede\">Call-center AI can support documentation and information access, but transcripts, summaries, suggestions, sentiment signals, and routing outputs can be incomplete or wrong. The employee remains responsible for the approved call workflow.</p><div class=\"module-meta\"><span><strong>Audience:</strong> Authorized call-center staff and supervisors</span><span><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Modules 1-5</span><span><strong>Level:</strong> Intermediate</span><span><strong>Evidence:</strong> Corrected call record</span></div><div class=\"warning custom-block\"><p class=\"custom-block-title\">Feature confirmation required</p><p>Teach only Genesys features enabled and approved for each DWIHN role. Confirm transcription, summarization, knowledge, sentiment, routing, recording, retention, and correction workflows before delivery.</p></div><h2 id=\"learning-objectives\" tabindex=\"-1\">Learning objectives <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#learning-objectives\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Learning objectives&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>By the end of this module, authorized learners can:</p><ul><li>Identify where enabled AI assistance appears in the call workflow.</li><li>Review a transcript for recognition errors and missing context.</li><li>Correct a summary using the approved source and process.</li><li>Evaluate knowledge suggestions before communicating them.</li><li>Treat sentiment and routing outputs as configured signals, not clinical facts.</li></ul><h2 id=\"module-content\" tabindex=\"-1\">Module content <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#module-content\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Module content&quot;\">​</a></h2><h3 id=\"_1-agent-assistance-and-suggestions\" tabindex=\"-1\">1. Agent assistance and suggestions <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#_1-agent-assistance-and-suggestions\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;1. Agent assistance and suggestions&quot;\">​</a></h3><p>Where enabled, agent assistance may surface information during a call. The employee must confirm that a suggestion matches the caller&#39;s question, comes from a current approved source, and is appropriate to communicate.</p><div class=\"tip custom-block\"><p class=\"custom-block-title\">Real-life example</p><p>A caller asks about a fictional service location. The system suggests an article, but the agent notices it describes a different program. The agent searches the approved knowledge source instead of reading the irrelevant suggestion.</p></div><h3 id=\"_2-transcripts-and-automatic-call-summaries\" tabindex=\"-1\">2. Transcripts and automatic call summaries <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#_2-transcripts-and-automatic-call-summaries\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;2. Transcripts and automatic call summaries&quot;\">​</a></h3><p>Speech recognition can mishear names, dates, numbers, accents, or specialized terms. A generated summary can omit open issues or turn a discussion into a commitment. Both require review before the call record is completed.</p><div class=\"tip custom-block\"><p class=\"custom-block-title\">Real-life example</p><p>A caller discusses a Thursday appointment but does not accept it. The generated summary says the appointment was booked. The agent corrects the summary to show that transportation must be confirmed first.</p></div><h3 id=\"_3-sentiment-alerts\" tabindex=\"-1\">3. Sentiment alerts <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#_3-sentiment-alerts\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;3. Sentiment alerts&quot;\">​</a></h3><p>Sentiment is an uncertain signal based on language or voice patterns. It may help an agent notice a possible change in a call, but it does not establish how a person feels, provide a diagnosis, or replace a required crisis procedure.</p><div class=\"tip custom-block\"><p class=\"custom-block-title\">Real-life example</p><p>The system displays a negative sentiment label while the caller calmly requests written confirmation. The agent responds to the caller&#39;s actual words and follows the approved workflow instead of treating the label as a clinical fact.</p></div><h3 id=\"_4-predictive-routing\" tabindex=\"-1\">4. Predictive routing <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#_4-predictive-routing\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;4. Predictive routing&quot;\">​</a></h3><p>Where predictive routing is enabled, the system may use configured information to direct a call. Staff should understand the routing purpose, their responsibility after receiving the call, and what to do when the route appears inappropriate.</p><div class=\"tip custom-block\"><p class=\"custom-block-title\">Real-life example</p><p>A call reaches a general queue even though the fictional caller needs language assistance. The agent follows the approved transfer or support process rather than assuming the routing decision cannot be changed.</p></div><h3 id=\"_5-using-the-approved-knowledge-base\" tabindex=\"-1\">5. Using the approved knowledge base <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#_5-using-the-approved-knowledge-base\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;5. Using the approved knowledge base&quot;\">​</a></h3><p>Knowledge suggestions are useful only when the content is relevant, current, and authorized. Employees should verify the article date, program, audience, and instructions before using it in a conversation.</p><div class=\"tip custom-block\"><p class=\"custom-block-title\">Real-life example</p><p>Two articles have similar titles, but only one contains the current fictional office hours. The agent checks the publication details and uses the current source.</p></div><h2 id=\"the-human-owned-call-workflow\" tabindex=\"-1\">The human-owned call workflow <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#the-human-owned-call-workflow\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;The human-owned call workflow&quot;\">​</a></h2><div class=\"workflow\"><div class=\"workflow-step\"><b>Receive</b><span>Follow authentication and opening procedures.</span></div><div class=\"workflow-step\"><b>Understand</b><span>Listen, clarify, and identify the reason for contact.</span></div><div class=\"workflow-step\"><b>Assist</b><span>Use current approved knowledge and procedures.</span></div><div class=\"workflow-step\"><b>Document</b><span>Review transcripts, notes, and proposed summaries.</span></div><div class=\"workflow-step\"><b>Confirm</b><span>Record agreed actions, open issues, and ownership.</span></div><div class=\"workflow-step\"><b>Follow up</b><span>Use the authorized route and required timeframe.</span></div></div><h2 id=\"what-enabled-ai-features-may-support\" tabindex=\"-1\">What enabled AI features may support <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#what-enabled-ai-features-may-support\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;What enabled AI features may support&quot;\">​</a></h2><div class=\"concept-grid\"><div class=\"concept-card\"><strong>Transcription</strong><p>Creates text from speech but may mishear names, numbers, accents, or specialized terms.</p></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><strong>Call summaries</strong><p>Propose a shorter record but may omit, combine, or overstate information.</p></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><strong>Knowledge suggestions</strong><p>Surface possible content that still requires relevance and currency checks.</p></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><strong>Signals and routing</strong><p>Support configured workflows but do not establish a diagnosis or replace procedure.</p></div></div><h2 id=\"story-booked-or-discussed\" tabindex=\"-1\">Story: booked or discussed? <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#story-booked-or-discussed\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Story: booked or discussed?&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>A fictional caller asks whether an appointment is available on Thursday. The agent explains the options, but the caller says they need to check transportation before choosing. The proposed summary states, &quot;Caller booked the Thursday appointment.&quot;</p><p>The summary converts a discussion into a commitment. The agent must correct the record before completing the approved documentation process.</p><h2 id=\"the-summary-review-checklist\" tabindex=\"-1\">The summary review checklist <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#the-summary-review-checklist\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;The summary review checklist&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>Confirm each item against the approved source:</p><ul><li>Reason for contact.</li><li>Important facts and barriers.</li><li>Information provided by the agent.</li><li>Decisions actually made.</li><li>Actions agreed to by each person.</li><li>Unresolved questions.</li><li>Follow-up owner and confirmed timeframe.</li><li>Any required escalation or documentation fields.</li></ul><h2 id=\"interactive-demonstration\" tabindex=\"-1\">Interactive demonstration <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#interactive-demonstration\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Interactive demonstration&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>Use a short fictional audio transcript and proposed summary:</p><ol><li>Mark transcript words that may have been misrecognized.</li><li>Compare each summary claim with the transcript.</li><li>Correct an overstatement and restore an omitted open question.</li><li>Check a knowledge suggestion against the approved source.</li><li>Complete the record using the confirmed DWIHN workflow.</li></ol><h2 id=\"hands-on-activity-correct-the-call-record\" tabindex=\"-1\">Hands-on activity: correct the call record <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#hands-on-activity-correct-the-call-record\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Hands-on activity: correct the call record&quot;\">​</a></h2><div class=\"learning-task\"><h3>Find what changed</h3><p>Review a fictional transcript and summary. Label each summary statement as <strong>supported</strong>, <strong>incomplete</strong>, <strong>incorrect</strong>, or <strong>unclear</strong>, then prepare a corrected version.</p></div><p>The exercise should include:</p><ul><li>One number transcribed incorrectly.</li><li>One action assigned to the wrong person.</li><li>One unresolved issue presented as resolved.</li><li>One important follow-up omitted from the summary.</li><li>One accurate statement that should remain unchanged.</li></ul><h2 id=\"sentiment-and-ethical-judgment\" tabindex=\"-1\">Sentiment and ethical judgment <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#sentiment-and-ethical-judgment\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Sentiment and ethical judgment&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>Sentiment analysis is an uncertain interpretation of language or voice patterns. It may be affected by culture, disability, communication style, background noise, or system limitations.</p><p>Do not use a sentiment label to diagnose a person, dismiss their stated need, or replace DWIHN&#39;s confirmed crisis and escalation procedures.</p><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\" tabindex=\"-1\">Common mistakes <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#common-mistakes\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Common mistakes&quot;\">​</a></h2><ul><li>Assuming the transcript is a perfect record.</li><li>Treating a generated summary as complete documentation.</li><li>Communicating a knowledge suggestion without checking it.</li><li>Treating sentiment as a clinical conclusion.</li><li>Allowing routing logic to override required employee actions.</li><li>Copying call information into an unauthorized tool or location.</li></ul><h2 id=\"mini-challenge\" tabindex=\"-1\">Mini challenge <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#mini-challenge\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Mini challenge&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>The sentiment indicator shows &quot;negative,&quot; but the caller calmly says they are satisfied and only need written confirmation. What should the agent do?</p><details class=\"details custom-block\"><summary>Suggested response</summary><p>Respond to the caller&#39;s words and the approved workflow. Treat the sentiment result as an uncertain signal, not as a clinical or factual conclusion. Document and follow up according to confirmed procedures.</p></details><h2 id=\"knowledge-check\" tabindex=\"-1\">Knowledge check <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#knowledge-check\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Knowledge check&quot;\">​</a></h2><ol><li>Why can a transcript contain errors?</li><li>What must be confirmed in a call summary?</li><li>How should a knowledge suggestion be used?</li><li>What does a sentiment signal establish?</li><li>Who owns the accuracy of the completed call record?</li></ol><details class=\"details custom-block\"><summary>Check your answers</summary><ol><li>Speech recognition may mishear words, numbers, names, accents, or background audio. 2. The reason for contact, facts, decisions, actions, open issues, follow-up, and required escalation. 3. Check its relevance, accuracy, currency, and approved use before communicating it. 4. It is an uncertain configured signal; it does not establish a diagnosis or replace procedure. 5. The authorized employee completing the approved workflow.</li></ol></details><div class=\"checkpoint\"><strong>Project evidence:</strong> Correct the continuing-case call summary and document the exact transcript evidence supporting each retained or changed statement.</div>", 53)
